{"annotations":{"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Lists the routes from one place to another: which stop to board, where to get off, the direction's destination, stops in between, and the walk at each end \u2014 best first, walking counted. Each end is a stop ID (`from_stop_id`) or coordinates (`from_lat` + `from_lng`), e.g. an address the user gave; a point covers every stop within a 600 m walk of it. `options` are direct routes. `transfer_options` have exactly one interchange (never more): ride `legs[0]`, walk `transfer_walk_meters` (within a 300 m stop cluster, 0 when it is the same stop) to `legs[1].board_stop`, ride `legs[1]`. They are listed when there is no direct route or when they beat the best direct one. Every option carries `schedule`: by the timetable, when to leave, when each leg boards and alights, when you arrive, and `total_minutes` door to door. Plan for now by default, or pass `depart_at` or `arrive_by` (\"HH:MM\" Lviv time today, or ISO 8601). When planning for now, options also carry `next_departures`: the live next departures of the first leg from its boarding stop, so no separate `get_stop_realtime` call is needed. `map_stops` holds the best trip's stops in riding order, each with a `role` (board, transfer \u2014 or transfer_alight + transfer_board when the interchange is a walk \u2014 and alight). Use when the user asks how to get from A to B, which bus/tram goes from one place to another, how long it takes, or when to leave to be somewhere on time. A stop end covers every stop within a 300 m walk of it, since a line's two directions often stop on opposite sides of a street under different names; `board_stop` says where to actually wait. Routes the city has suspended, and stops a detour skips, are left out. `walk_meters` is set when the two ends are within a 300 m walk of each other: no ride is searched then, so tell the user to walk. Otherwise both lists empty means the trip needs two or more transfers. Get stop IDs with `search_stops` or `get_stops_around_location`.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","properties":{"arrive_by":{"description":"Arrive by this time: \"HH:MM\" Lviv time today, or ISO 8601. Not together with `depart_at`.","type":"string"},"depart_at":{"description":"Leave at this time: \"HH:MM\" Lviv time today, or ISO 8601. Default now. Not together with `arrive_by`.","type":"string"},"from_lat":{"description":"Decimal latitude of the start point, WGS84 (e.g. 49.842 for central Lviv).","maximum":90,"minimum":-90,"type":"number"},"from_lng":{"description":"Decimal longitude of the start point, WGS84 (e.g. 24.031 for central Lviv).","maximum":180,"minimum":-180,"type":"number"},"from_stop_id":{"description":"Stop ID where the trip starts. Give this or `from_lat` + `from_lng`.","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991,"type":"integer"},"to_lat":{"description":"Decimal latitude of the destination, WGS84 (e.g. 49.842 for central Lviv).","maximum":90,"minimum":-90,"type":"number"},"to_lng":{"description":"Decimal longitude of the destination, WGS84 (e.g. 24.031 for central Lviv).","maximum":180,"minimum":-180,"type":"number"},"to_stop_id":{"description":"Stop ID where the trip ends. Give this or `to_lat` + `to_lng`.","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991,"type":"integer"}},"type":"object"},"name":"find_routes_between","outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"data":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"disruptions":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"alternatives":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"name":{"type":"string"}},"required":["name","id"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"detour":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"skipped_stops":{"items":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":-9007199254740991,"type"